<task id="050" project="messaging-communication-app-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>BFF thread-read + unread-count endpoints (access-filtered per FR-08)</title>
    <phase>W5 — BFF Endpoints</phase>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <estimated-hours>6</estimated-hours>
    <dependencies>040,042,004</dependencies>
    <blocks>060</blocks>
    <tags>bff-api, communication</tags>
    <rigor-hint>FULL</rigor-hint>
    <rigor-reason>Adds two new BFF endpoints to `Sprk.Bff.Api` that drive the ~5s poll and MUST enforce FR-08 privacy/internal-only/privilege filtering on every read (NFR-06 security-sensitive downstream of 042). BFF-touching: publish-size + CVE + bff-extensions Placement Justification required; access-filter correctness demands code-review + adr-check at Step 9.5.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>W5</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <fr-refs>FR-11, NFR-07</fr-refs>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Add two BFF read endpoints that drive the polling timeline (task 060) over the thread model:

    • **Thread-read** — return a thread's `sprk_communication` rows for rendering: `sprk_body` + `sprk_bodyformat`, channel type (`sprk_communicationtype`), sender, timestamp, reply-parent pointer (`sprk_inreplyto`), and attachment references (`sprk_document` links via the `sprk_communicationattachment` intersection). Ordered, groupable by `sprk_thread`.
    • **Unread-count** — return the count of messages in a thread (or across the caller's authorized threads, per the read model chosen) that are newer than the caller's last-seen marker.

    **BOTH endpoints MUST be access-filtered per FR-08** — they return ONLY messages the caller may read: record-scoped (open) threads via `MembershipResolverService` (ADR-034)-derived access, private threads via the per-record sharing grant, message-level privacy + internal-only + privilege composed exactly as the task-042 BFF query-filter enforces. The unread count reflects only messages the caller may read, since the caller's last-seen. Reuse the task-042 filter path — do NOT author a second, divergent filter. Both endpoints MUST be **lightweight** to bound poll load at ~5s cadence (NFR-07): projected/paged reads, no per-row fan-out, no ACS call (Dataverse is the record). No client-side ACS SDK is involved (server read only).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF engineer for the Communication subsystem. Authority on `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/` endpoints + `Services/Communication/`. Fluent in ADR-008 (endpoint filters), ADR-003 (authorization seams), ADR-019 (ProblemDetails), ADR-024 (regarding family / thread anchor), the FR-08 privacy model (task 042), NFR-07 (bound poll load), `docs/standards/DATA-ACCESS-DECISION-CRITERIA.md` (BFF read vs `Xrm.WebApi`), §10 BFF Hygiene, and §11 Component Justification.
  </role>

  <goal>
    Two BFF endpoints exist — thread-read (a thread's messages with body/channel/sender/attachments) and unread-count (since caller's last-seen) — both routing reads through the task-042 access-filter so a caller sees ONLY authorized messages, private/internal-only/privileged content never leaks, and unread reflects only readable messages. Reads are lightweight (projected/paged, no ACS call) to bound ~5s poll load (NFR-07). Endpoints carry ADR-008 filters + ADR-019 ProblemDetails, are registered unconditionally, and drive task 060. Build clean; endpoint + access-filter tests pass; publish-size delta + CVE + bff-extensions Placement Justification reported.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      The polling conversation/timeline component (task 060, FR-10) reads persisted `sprk_communication` rows from the BFF and polls a thread-read endpoint on a ~5s interval; an unread indicator polls an unread-count endpoint (design §6.2). Neither endpoint exists today — the current communication surface is a flat OOB subgrid + one-record-at-a-time form (design §2). These two reads are the server read model for the whole R1 UI.

      Component Justification (§11): (1) Existing — no endpoint returns a thread's messages grouped by `sprk_thread` with attachment references, and no unread-count endpoint exists (grep-verify before claiming). The task-042 filter enforces privacy but exposes no read endpoint; existing communication endpoints are send/regarding-review, not thread-read. (2) Extension — these are additive read endpoints on the existing communication `Api/` surface reusing the task-042 filter path; they do NOT introduce a new service or a second filter. (3) Cost-of-doing-nothing (concrete): without the thread-read endpoint the timeline component has nothing to render and no way to reflect a newly-captured inbound message within a poll cycle (FR-10/FR-11 acceptance fails); without access-filtering on these reads, a private/internal-only/privileged message leaks to an unauthorized caller (NFR-06 security failure). These are named contract failures, not "future flexibility."

      NFR-07 discipline: at ~5s cadence with many concurrent open forms, an unbounded read or per-row fan-out floods the BFF. Keep reads projected (only the columns the timeline needs), paged, and free of ACS calls (Dataverse is the record — no ACS read needed to view/sync history, design §6.2). Tune/monitor; escalate to spine push (R2) only if load warrants.

      Privacy is the load-bearing correctness property (FR-08 / NFR-06). Task 042 owns the BFF query-filter that composes message-level + thread-level privacy, internal-only (D-05 user attribute), and privilege classification over `MembershipResolverService`-derived access. This task MUST consume that filter, not re-derive access. Point-forward semantics (a thread flipped to open exposes only messages from that point forward) come from the filter, not from these endpoints.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ (communication endpoints — add thread-read + unread-count here)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/CommunicationService.cs</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/ (task-042 privacy query-filter; task-040 IThreadResolver / sprk_thread lookup)</file>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/CommunicationModule.cs (endpoint + service registration)</file>
      <file>docs/standards/DATA-ACCESS-DECISION-CRITERIA.md (BFF read for the timeline vs Xrm.WebApi)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-11">Thread-read returns a thread's `sprk_communication` rows (`sprk_body`, channel type, sender, attachments); unread-count returns messages since the caller's last-seen. BOTH access-filtered.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-08 / NFR-06">Both endpoints return ONLY messages the caller may read: open via `MembershipResolverService` (ADR-034), private via per-record sharing grant, message/thread privacy + internal-only + privilege composed via the task-042 filter. No privileged/private/internal-only content leaks. Reuse the 042 filter path; do NOT author a second filter. Point-forward privacy honored.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-07">Lightweight to bound ~5s poll load: projected columns only, paged, no per-row fan-out, NO ACS call (Dataverse is the record). Tunable/monitorable.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">Both endpoints carry the standard authorization endpoint filter; auth posture consistent with the communication surface.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">Authorization derives from the canonical authorization seams / Dataverse-derived access — never a bespoke ACL.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">Errors (thread not found, forbidden, bad request) return RFC 7807 ProblemDetails.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-024">Thread anchor uses the existing regarding family via `sprk_communicationthread`; MUST NOT add a second regarding mechanism.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-032 / ADR-018">Endpoints registered unconditionally; any feature-gated dependency uses the Null-Object pattern (no asymmetric registration).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">Inject central `TokenCredential` + canonical Dataverse interfaces; MUST NOT `new` a credential.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-04">Server read only — MUST NOT import or introduce any client-side ACS SDK.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">§11 Component Justification: state the concrete FR-11/NFR-06 failure modes prevented. §10 bff-extensions Placement Justification in the PR; publish-size delta vs ~45.30 MB baseline; no new HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

