    <patterns>
      <pattern name="Access-filtered communication read" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/">
        Route both reads through the task-042 BFF query-filter so open/private/internal-only/privilege access is composed once; the endpoint never re-derives access.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="Thread grouping query" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/">
        Timeline query = filter `sprk_communication` where `sprk_thread` = X (design §6.1); projected columns only; paged; ordered for interleave + reply nesting.
      </pattern>
      <pattern name="ProblemDetails endpoint" location="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/">
        ADR-019 ProblemDetails on error; ADR-008 authorization endpoint filter; unconditional mapping (ADR-032).
      </pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps>
    <step order="1">Read `docs/standards/DATA-ACCESS-DECISION-CRITERIA.md` (confirms BFF read for the timeline, not `Xrm.WebApi`) + `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` §F/§G + §11 Component Justification before adding endpoints.</step>
    <step order="2">Read the task-042 privacy query-filter + the task-040 `IThreadResolver` / `sprk_thread` lookup + the task-004 thread schema to identify the exact filter entry point to reuse and the `sprk_communication` columns to project.</step>
    <step order="3">Grep the existing communication `Api/` surface to confirm no thread-read or unread-count endpoint exists (§11 existing-question evidence).</step>
    <step order="4">Implement the thread-read endpoint: input = thread id (+ optional paging/since cursor); route through the task-042 access-filter; project `sprk_body`, `sprk_bodyformat`, `sprk_communicationtype`, sender, timestamp, `sprk_inreplyto`, and attachment references (`sprk_document` via `sprk_communicationattachment`); ordered + paged. No ACS call.</step>
    <step order="5">Implement the unread-count endpoint: count access-filtered messages newer than the caller's last-seen marker (define the last-seen source — per-caller marker; scope to the thread or authorized threads per the read model). Lightweight aggregate, no row materialization.</step>
    <step order="6">Apply ADR-008 authorization endpoint filter + ADR-019 ProblemDetails (not-found / forbidden / bad-request) to both endpoints; register both unconditionally via `CommunicationModule` (ADR-010/ADR-032).</step>
    <step order="7">Write tests: (a) thread-read returns a thread's messages with body/channel/sender/attachment refs; (b) a caller WITHOUT access to a private thread receives NONE of its messages (negative); (c) an internal-only message is absent for a non-internal caller (negative); (d) a privileged message is filtered per the 042 filter (negative); (e) unread-count reflects only readable messages since last-seen and excludes a private/internal-only message the caller can't read (negative); (f) reads are projected/paged (no unbounded fetch) — NFR-07 shape assertion.</step>
    <step order="8">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` + `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ --filter Communication`; confirm existing communication tests still pass.</step>
    <step order="9.1">Run `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o deploy/api-publish/`; report compressed size + delta vs ~45.30 MB baseline. Expected ≈ 0 (no new packages).</step>
    <step order="9.2">Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — confirm no new HIGH-severity CVEs.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates: `code-review` on the diff (focus access-filter correctness / no-leak); `adr-check` against `spec.md` (focus FR-08/NFR-06 filtering, ADR-008/003/019, §11 justification, NFR-07 bound load). Address Critical findings; cite bff-extensions Placement Justification.</step>
    <step order="10">Run `/conflict-check` before the PR (BFF hot-path; shared `Services/Communication/`; coordinate with `notification-spine-r1`).</step>
    <step order="11">Update `tasks/TASK-INDEX.md` (050 ✅) + `current-task.md`; record decisions (read-model scope, last-seen source, filter-reuse entry point, paging shape).</step>
  </steps>

