  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A thread-read endpoint returns a thread's `sprk_communication` rows including `sprk_body`, `sprk_bodyformat`, channel type, sender, timestamp, `sprk_inreplyto`, and attachment references — ordered and filterable by `sprk_thread`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">An unread-count endpoint returns the count of readable messages newer than the caller's last-seen marker.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Both endpoints route through the task-042 access-filter — no second/divergent filter is introduced (grep/diff-verifiable).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: a caller without a grant to a private thread receives NONE of its messages from thread-read, and the private messages are NOT counted in unread-count.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: an internal-only message is absent from thread-read and excluded from unread-count for a non-internal caller.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: a privileged message is filtered exactly as the 042 filter dictates (no leak beyond the composed access set).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Reads are projected + paged and make NO ACS call (NFR-07 bound poll load; server read only, no ACS SDK import).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Both endpoints carry the ADR-008 authorization filter + ADR-019 ProblemDetails and are registered unconditionally (ADR-032).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet build` clean; publish-size delta ≈ 0 vs ~45.30 MB; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Depends on 040 (`sprk_thread` lookup / `IThreadResolver`), 042 (the access-filter this endpoint MUST reuse), and 004 (thread schema). Blocks 060 (the timeline component consumes both endpoints). The single most important correctness property is no-leak: the negative access-filter cases are non-negotiable (NFR-06, security-sensitive). If reusing the 042 filter would force a change to it, coordinate — do NOT fork a parallel filter into the endpoint.

    NFR-07: these two reads are the ~5s poll surface for every open form. Keep them cheap by construction (projection + paging + no ACS). Note monitoring hooks in the PR so poll load is observable; spine-push escalation is an R2 concern, not R1.
  </notes>

